B.cyn={"i'm at the hospital":0,"help me talk to my doctor":1,"what should i ask before i leave":2,"i feel like they're not listening":3,"help me advocate for myself":4,"i need a script to say right now":5,"i'm overwhelmed":6,"i need help right now":7}
B.HT=new A.aq(B.cyn,['That sounds stressful \u2014 I\'m right here with you \ud83d\udc9c\n\nHere\'s what you can do right now:\n\n**Ask these questions:**\n\u2022 "Can you explain what\'s happening and what the plan is?"\n\u2022 "What are the warning signs I should watch for?"\n\u2022 "What should I do if my symptoms get worse after I leave?"\n\n**If you\'re being discharged and feel unsure:**\n\u2022 "I don\'t feel fully comfortable leaving without understanding the plan. Can we go over it together?"\n\u2022 "Can you document my concern and the plan in my chart?"\n\nWhat specifically is happening right now? Tell me more and I\'ll help you with exactly what to say.','Of course \u2014 let\'s prepare you \ud83c\udf38\n\n**Before you go in, think about:**\n\u2022 What is your main concern today?\n\u2022 When did it start and how often does it happen?\n\u2022 How severe is it on a scale of 1\u201310?\n\u2022 What makes it better or worse?\n\n**Useful phrases:**\n\u2022 "I\'m most concerned about..."\n\u2022 "I\'d like to make sure we talk about..."\n\u2022 "I\'ve also noticed..."\n\u2022 "I\'d like to understand what this means for my pregnancy."\n\n**If you feel rushed:**\n\u2022 "I have a few more questions \u2014 can we take a moment?"\n\u2022 "Can I get a printed summary of today\'s visit?"\n\nWhat are you going in for? I can help you prepare specific questions.','Great instinct \u2014 don\'t leave without these answers \ud83d\udccb\n\n**Discharge checklist \u2014 ask your provider:**\n1. **Diagnosis / plan**: "What is your assessment and what\'s the plan?"\n2. **Warning signs**: "What specific symptoms mean I should come back immediately?"\n3. **Follow-up**: "When should I follow up and with whom?"\n4. **Medications**: "Are there any changes I should know about?"\n5. **Activity**: "Are there any restrictions I should follow?"\n6. **Baby**: "Is everything okay with the baby right now?"\n\n**If anything is unclear:**\n\u2022 "Can you say that again in simpler terms?"\n\u2022 "Can I get this in writing?"\n\u2022 "Can this be noted in my chart?"\n\nIs there something specific that\'s unclear right now?','I hear you \u2014 that\'s a really hard feeling, and it\'s valid \ud83d\udc9c\n\n**Calm, clear ways to get your concern heard:**\n\u2022 *"I want to make sure my concern is documented. Can we note this in my chart?"*\n\u2022 *"I\'m still concerned and I\'d like to understand why this isn\'t being recommended."*\n\u2022 *"What would need to change for this to become a priority?"*\n\n**If you need to escalate:**\n\u2022 "Is there another provider, a charge nurse, or a supervisor who can review this with me?"\n\u2022 "Can I request a patient advocate?"\n\nYou have the right to ask questions and seek clarification. Advocating for yourself is necessary, not rude.\n\nWhat specifically are they not responding to? I can help you phrase it exactly.','You\'re doing the right thing \ud83c\udf38\n\n**Self-advocacy toolkit:**\n1. **Name your concern**: "I am concerned about [specific symptom/issue]."\n2. **Ask for reasoning**: "Can you help me understand why this approach is recommended?"\n3. **Request documentation**: "Can this concern and the plan be noted in my chart?"\n4. **Ask about alternatives**: "Are there other options we could consider?"\n5. **Ask about warning signs**: "What should bring me back immediately?"\n6. **Request clarification**: "I want to make sure I understand before I leave."\n\n**If you feel dismissed:**\nStay calm \u2014 a composed tone is more effective. Be specific about what you need. Request documentation. Ask for a patient advocate or charge nurse if needed.\n\nWhat\'s the situation? I can give you specific language.',"Here's a simple script you can read out loud right now:\n\n---\n*\"I want to make sure I understand what's happening. My main concern is [what you're worried about]. I'd like to know what you think is causing this, what the plan is, and what warning signs mean I should come back. I'd also appreciate if my concern could be noted in my chart.\"*\n\n---\n\n**Shorter version:**\n*\"I'm still concerned. Can you explain the reasoning and what I should watch for?\"*\n\nTell me what's specifically happening and I'll write you a more tailored script in seconds.","Take a breath \u2014 I'm with you \ud83d\udc9c\n\nYou don't have to figure everything out right now. Let's take it one step at a time.\n\n**Right now, just tell me:**\nWhat is the one thing that feels most urgent or scary?\n\nI'll help you with exactly that. You don't have to have all the words \u2014 that's what I'm here for.","I'm here. Take a breath \ud83d\udc9c\n\nTell me what's happening and I'll guide you through it step by step. You don't need to explain everything at once \u2014 just start with what feels most urgent."],t.w)
