B.daG=new A.jS(B.a3f,2,5,"Congestion has shown up more than once this week. Mild nasal congestion is common in babies, but keep watching feeding, sleep, and breathing effort. (AAP/CDC)","Congestion is showing up frequently. Contact your pediatrician if it is worsening or affecting breathing, feeding, or sleep. (AAP/CDC)","Congestion has been logged, but the pattern is still limited. Continue monitoring for changes in breathing, feeding, and comfort. (AAP/CDC)","Mild congestion can be common in babies, especially with dry air or minor viral symptoms, but it should not make breathing look hard. Use saline drops and gentle suction if needed, and watch for poor feeding, fever, retractions, fast breathing, or color change. Contact your pediatrician sooner if congestion recurs, worsens, or disrupts sleep or feeding.","AAP / CDC infant respiratory guidance")
B.a1E=s(["cough","coughing"],t.s)
B.daF=new A.jS(B.a1E,2,4,"Cough has shown up repeatedly. Track whether it is disturbing sleep, feeds, or happens with congestion or fever. (AAP/CDC)","Cough is appearing frequently. Contact your pediatrician if it is worsening, persistent, or paired with breathing trouble, fever, or poor feeding. (AAP/CDC)","Cough has been logged and is now being tracked for pattern changes. (AAP/CDC)","Occasional cough can happen with saliva, reflux, or mild viral irritation, but persistent cough in a young baby deserves closer attention. Watch for breathing effort, pauses, fever, vomiting, or trouble feeding. Contact your pediatrician sooner if cough is frequent, worsening, or affecting sleep or intake.","AAP / CDC infant respiratory guidance")
B.c29=s(["runny nose","nasal drainage","runny_nose"],t.s)
B.daO=new A.jS(B.c29,2,5,"Runny nose is recurring this week. Mild nasal drainage is common, but watch for fever, feeding difficulty, or thick worsening mucus. (AAP/CDC)","Runny nose is showing up frequently. Contact your pediatrician if it is worsening or affecting breathing, feeding, or sleep. (AAP/CDC)","Runny nose has been logged and is being tracked over time. (AAP/CDC)","A mild runny nose can happen with dry air or viral irritation, but babies can struggle when nasal symptoms interfere with feeding or rest. Use gentle suction or saline if needed, and watch for fever, labored breathing, dehydration, or a big change in comfort. Contact your pediatrician sooner if symptoms persist or intensify.","AAP / CDC infant respiratory guidance")
B.a3A=s(["sneezing","sneeze"],t.s)
B.daI=new A.jS(B.a3A,3,6,"Sneezing has shown up on multiple days. Occasional sneezing is common in babies, but keep watching if it clusters with congestion, cough, or feeding changes. (AAP)","Sneezing is showing up very frequently. Contact your pediatrician if it is worsening or happening alongside congestion, fever, or feeding trouble. (AAP)","Sneezing has been logged and is now being tracked. Occasional sneezing can be normal in babies. (AAP)","Sneezing by itself is often normal in babies and can help clear little noses, especially around dust or dry air. What matters more is whether it starts pairing with congestion, fever, poor feeding, or breathing effort. Keep tracking the pattern and contact your pediatrician if it becomes persistent or comes with other symptoms.","AAP infant care guidance")
B.Zq=s(["difficulty breathing","breathing trouble","labored breathing"],t.s)
B.daE=new A.jS(B.Zq,1,1,"Breathing difficulty should never be treated as routine in a baby. This needs prompt medical attention. (AAP/CDC)","Breathing difficulty in a baby is urgent. Seek immediate medical care now. (AAP/CDC)","No breathing difficulty pattern has been logged.","Fast breathing, pulling in at the ribs, grunting, flaring nostrils, pauses, or color change are red flags in babies. Do not wait to see if this resolves on its own. Seek urgent medical evaluation immediately if breathing ever looks hard or abnormal.","AAP / CDC infant respiratory guidance")
B.a1F=s(["rash","skin rash"],t.s)
B.daK=new A.jS(B.a1F,2,5,"Rash has shown up more than once. Many newborn rashes are mild, but keep tracking whether it spreads, blisters, or seems uncomfortable. (AAP/NHS)","Rash is recurring frequently. Contact your pediatrician if it is worsening, widespread, blistering, or paired with fever. (AAP/NHS)","Rash has been logged and is now being tracked over time. (AAP/NHS)","Many newborn rashes are short-lived and harmless, but the pattern matters. Watch for fever, facial swelling, blisters, pus, pain, or rapid spread. Contact your pediatrician sooner if the rash worsens, keeps returning, or makes your baby seem uncomfortable.","AAP / NHS newborn skin guidance")
B.Y2=s(["dry skin","dry skin / peeling","peeling skin"],t.s)
B.daH=new A.jS(B.Y2,3,7,"Dry or peeling skin is recurring, but this is often common in newborns. Keep watching for cracking, bleeding, or signs of irritation. (AAP)","Dry or peeling skin is lingering. Contact your pediatrician if skin is cracking deeply, bleeding, or looks infected. (AAP)","Dry or peeling skin has been logged and is being tracked. Mild peeling can be normal in newborns. (AAP)","Mild peeling is often normal in newborn skin. Use gentle fragrance-free care and avoid overbathing, and watch for redness, oozing, cracking, or signs of discomfort. Contact your pediatrician sooner if skin changes are severe, infected-looking, or not improving.","AAP newborn skin care guidance")
B.a2U=s(["eye discharge","goopy eye","watery eye"],t.s)
B.daJ=new A.jS(B.a2U,2,5,"Eye discharge has shown up repeatedly. Mild tear-duct blockage can be common, but watch for redness, swelling, or worsening drainage. (AAP/NHS)","Eye discharge is recurring frequently. Contact your pediatrician if the eye looks red, swollen, painful, or the drainage is thickening. (AAP/NHS)","Eye discharge has been logged and is now being tracked. (AAP/NHS)","A small amount of eye discharge can happen with a blocked tear duct, especially if the white of the eye still looks calm. Redness, swelling, fever, or thick yellow-green discharge are more concerning. Contact your pediatrician sooner if the eye looks irritated or the drainage keeps returning.","AAP / NHS infant eye guidance")
B.a3D=s(["swelling","swollen"],t.s)
B.daP=new A.jS(B.a3D,1,3,"Swelling has been logged. Track where it is, whether it is improving, and whether it affects feeding, movement, or comfort. (AAP)","Swelling is recurring or persistent. Contact your pediatrician promptly, especially if it is worsening, red, or painful. (AAP)","Swelling has been logged and is now being tracked. (AAP)","Mild temporary swelling can happen in some situations, but persistent or worsening swelling deserves closer attention. Watch for redness, heat, pain, asymmetry, poor movement, or a major change in comfort. Contact your pediatrician sooner if swelling persists, returns, or seems to be increasing.","AAP infant symptom guidance")
B.Zo=s(["gas","gassy","gas / gassiness"],t.s)
B.daN=new A.jS(B.Zo,3,6,"Gas has shown up on multiple days. Gassiness is common in babies, but keep tracking whether it is affecting sleep, crying, or feeding comfort. (AAP)","Gas symptoms are showing up frequently. Contact your pediatrician if discomfort is worsening, severe, or paired with vomiting, poor feeding, or blood in stool. (AAP)","Gas has been logged and is now being tracked. Mild gassiness is common in babies. (AAP)","Gassiness is common in babies and often improves with time, feeding-position changes, or burping. What matters more is whether your baby seems hard to console, feeds poorly, vomits, or has stool changes. Contact your pediatrician sooner if the discomfort seems severe or is paired with other concerning symptoms.","AAP infant feeding guidance")
B.a1D=s(["constipation","constipated"],t.s)
B.daD=new A.jS(B.a1D,2,5,"Constipation has shown up more than once. Stool timing can vary in babies, but hard stools, straining, or discomfort are worth tracking. (AAP)","Constipation is recurring frequently. Contact your pediatrician if stools are hard, painful, bloody, or your baby is feeding poorly. (AAP)","Constipation has been logged and is now being tracked. (AAP)","Baby stool frequency can vary a lot, especially between feeding types and ages, so timing alone is not the whole story. Hard pellet-like stools, blood, marked straining, or poor feeding are more concerning. Contact your pediatrician sooner if constipation keeps returning or causes significant discomfort.","AAP infant stool guidance")
B.a2r=s(["diarrhea","diarrhoea","loose stools"],t.s)
B.daM=new A.jS(B.a2r,2,4,"Diarrhea has shown up repeatedly. Watch hydration closely and note whether stools are much looser or more frequent than usual. (AAP/CDC)","Diarrhea is recurring frequently. Contact your pediatrician if there are signs of dehydration, blood, fever, or poor feeding. (AAP/CDC)","Diarrhea has been logged and is now being tracked. (AAP/CDC)","Because baby stools vary naturally, the most helpful clue is a sudden shift to much looser, more frequent stools than normal for your baby. Watch for fewer wet diapers, dry mouth, fever, blood, or unusual sleepiness. Contact your pediatrician sooner if diarrhea persists or hydration seems affected.","AAP / CDC infant diarrhea guidance")
B.a3m=s(["reflux","arching","reflux / arching"],t.s)
B.daL=new A.jS(B.a3m,2,5,"Reflux or arching has shown up on multiple days. Mild spit-up can be normal, but track whether it is affecting comfort, feeds, or weight gain. (AAP)","Reflux or arching is recurring frequently. Contact your pediatrician if symptoms are worsening or paired with projectile vomiting, poor feeding, choking, or poor weight gain. (AAP)","Reflux or arching has been logged and is now being tracked. (AAP)","Many babies spit up or arch sometimes, especially after feeds, and mild reflux often improves with time. More concerning signs include projectile vomiting, choking, feeding refusal, blood, or poor growth. Contact your pediatrician sooner if reflux-like symptoms are becoming frequent or interfering with comfort or feeding.","AAP infant reflux guidance")
