B.azn=new A.k(1,1,0.6039215686274509,0.7843137254901961,B.q)
B.bGR=s(["Add your due date or weeks pregnant in Profile for tailored weekly guidance."],t.s)
B.buY=s(["Movement timing varies. Your guide will personalize once the week is known."],t.s)
B.b7r=s(["Track symptoms, nutrition, mood, appointments, and questions for your care team."],t.s)
B.bIC=s(["Continue prenatal vitamins if recommended, hydrate, and aim for balanced meals."],t.s)
B.bk1=s(["Use appointments to ask about symptoms, nutrition, medications, fetal movement, and next milestones."],t.s)
B.c21=s(["Heavy bleeding, severe pain, fainting, fever, chest pain, severe headache/vision changes, or anything that feels urgent."],t.s)
B.aib=new A.ps("Pregnancy Journey","Add your due date or weeks pregnant for week-specific guidance","Week-specific size appears here","\u2014","\u2014","Pregnancy overview",B.v6,B.azn,B.bGR,B.buY,B.b7r,B.bIC,B.bk1,B.c21)
B.aDU=new A.k(1,1,0.7607843137254902,0.43529411764705883,B.q)
B.bLD=s(["Lungs are developing air sacs and early surfactant production begins over this period.","Skin is still thin but becoming less translucent as fat stores slowly build.","Taste buds develop, and baby swallows amniotic fluid regularly."],t.s)
B.bLw=s(["Hearing is improving; baby may react to voices, music, or sudden sounds.","Kicks, rolls, and stretches can become more noticeable, especially when resting."],t.s)
B.bZC=s(["Leg cramps, reflux, constipation, Braxton Hicks, and pelvic/back discomfort can appear.","Sleep may need pillows or side-lying support.","Mood and body-image shifts are common; support matters."],t.s)
B.bQn=s(["Balanced meals with protein/fiber can help energy and blood-sugar steadiness.","Calcium, vitamin D, magnesium, potassium, and fluids can support bones and cramp prevention discussions.","Continue safe seafood choices for omega-3s while avoiding high-mercury fish."],t.s)
B.bOI=s(["Glucose screening planning commonly happens soon, depending on your care schedule.","Review movement expectations, blood pressure, swelling, and pain symptoms."],t.s)
B.bOO=s(["Regular painful contractions, pelvic pressure, bleeding, fluid leakage, or severe backache before term.","Severe headache, vision changes, right-upper abdominal pain, sudden swelling, chest pain, or shortness of breath."],t.s)
B.aic=new A.ps("Weeks 21\u201324: Senses waking up","Second trimester \xb7 hearing, movement & growth","Corn cob / cantaloupe","10.5\u201312 in head-to-heel","12\u201321 oz","A slender fetus with more active movements in fluid",B.Do,B.aDU,B.bLD,B.bLw,B.bZC,B.bQn,B.bOI,B.bOO)
B.awk=new A.k(1,0.4235294117647059,0.4823529411764706,1,B.q)
B.aB5=new A.k(1,1,0.7058823529411765,0.37254901960784315,B.q)
B.bLb=s(["The anatomy ultrasound often checks brain, heart, spine, organs, limbs, placenta, fluid, and growth.","Vernix begins protecting the skin, and fine lanugo hair may be present.","Baby\u2019s proportions become more balanced as limbs lengthen."],t.s)
B.c_X=s(["Many people begin feeling flutters between 18\u201322 weeks, though placenta position matters.","Baby can hear more internal body sounds and may respond to movement or pressure."],t.s)
B.bGr=s(["Backache, hip discomfort, round-ligament pain, reflux, and sleep-position changes are common.","You may notice a clearer bump and changes in balance/posture.","Movement can feel irregular at first and usually becomes more consistent later."],t.s)
B.bIL=s(["Iron needs rise as blood volume expands; pair plant iron with vitamin C foods.","Omega-3-rich low-mercury fish, choline, iodine, calcium, and vitamin D may be worth discussing.","Keep water intake steady, especially with constipation or headaches."],t.s)
B.bXS=s(["Review anatomy scan findings and any follow-up imaging recommendations.","Ask about fetal movement expectations, pelvic floor support, and glucose screening timing."],t.s)
B.c_9=s(["Bleeding, leaking fluid, severe abdominal pain, fever, severe headache/vision symptoms, or chest pain.","Painful urination, one-sided swelling/pain, or symptoms that feel escalating."],t.s)
B.aid=new A.ps("Weeks 17\u201320: Anatomy scan season","Second trimester \xb7 movement may begin","Bell pepper / banana","5.1\u20136.5 in","5\u201311 oz","A curled fetus with visible fingers, toes, and facial profile",B.awk,B.aB5,B.bLb,B.c_X,B.bGr,B.bIL,B.bXS,B.c_9)
B.azR=new A.k(1,0.21568627450980393,0.7254901960784313,0.5568627450980392,B.q)
B.azi=new A.k(1,1,0.43529411764705883,0.5686274509803921,B.q)
B.bKo=s(["Baby continues gaining weight and preparing for temperature regulation, feeding, and breathing after birth.","The brain keeps developing rapidly through the final weeks and beyond birth.","Vernix and fat stores help protect skin and support newborn transition."],t.s)
B.bkV=s(["Movement may feel like firm rolls, stretches, and pressure rather than big flips.","Any meaningful decrease from baby\u2019s usual pattern should be checked promptly."],t.s)
B.bN4=s(["Lightening, pelvic pressure, mucus plug changes, irregular contractions, and backache may happen.","True labor contractions tend to become regular, stronger, longer, and closer together.","Rest, hydration, and clear support plans matter now."],t.s)
B.bFW=s(["Keep easy, nourishing meals/snacks available for late pregnancy and early postpartum.","Hydrate and include protein/fiber to support energy and digestion.","Discuss any diabetes, blood pressure, anemia, or special diet needs with your clinician."],t.s)
B.bMD=s(["Review labor signs, when to go in, induction/post-dates planning, fetal monitoring, and postpartum support.","Confirm newborn feeding, pediatric care, safe sleep, and emergency contacts."],t.s)
B.c_H=s(["Reduced movement, heavy bleeding, green/brown fluid, severe headache/vision changes, chest pain, or severe abdominal pain.","Fever, difficulty breathing, seizure, or any symptom your care team told you is urgent."],t.s)
B.aie=new A.ps("Weeks 37\u201342: Full-term window","Third trimester \xb7 birth can be close","Watermelon / newborn size","19\u201321+ in head-to-heel","6\u20139+ lb","A full-term baby curled head-down, ready for birth",B.azR,B.azi,B.bKo,B.bkV,B.bN4,B.bFW,B.bMD,B.c_H)
B.ay3=new A.k(1,0.23137254901960785,0.6196078431372549,1,B.q)
B.aAf=new A.k(1,1,0.6078431372549019,0.45098039215686275,B.q)
B.bNc=s(["Eyes may begin opening, and sleep/wake cycles become more organized.","The brain is adding folds and connections quickly.","Fat gain increases, helping temperature regulation after birth."],t.s)
B.bkf=s(["Movements are usually more obvious and may form familiar daily patterns.","Baby may respond to light, sound, meals, or your resting position."],t.s)
B.bQG=s(["Shortness of breath, reflux, swelling, back/pelvic pain, and sleep disruption may increase.","Braxton Hicks can happen, but regular painful contractions should be checked.","Blood pressure and swelling awareness become increasingly important."],t.s)
B.b7t=s(["Iron, protein, calcium, vitamin D, choline, folate, fiber, and fluids remain key.","If glucose screening is abnormal, nutrition guidance should be individualized by your care team.","Pair carbs with protein/fat/fiber to support steadier energy."],t.s)
B.bel=s(["Review glucose screening, anemia screening, vaccines, Rh status if relevant, and third-trimester visit frequency.","Ask when to start formal kick-count guidance and what pattern changes mean."],t.s)
B.be9=s(["Reduced or concerning movement pattern, bleeding, leaking fluid, regular contractions, or severe abdominal pain.",u.bR],t.s)
B.aif=new A.ps("Weeks 25\u201328: Third trimester doorway","Late second / early third trimester \xb7 growth accelerating","Cauliflower / eggplant","13\u201314.8 in head-to-heel","1.5\u20132.2 lb","A fetus filling more of the womb, with stronger kicks",B.ay3,B.aAf,B.bNc,B.bkf,B.bQG,B.b7t,B.bel,B.be9)
B.aBa=new A.k(1,0.6235294117647059,0.4196078431372549,1,B.q)
B.aA7=new A.k(1,1,0.6235294117647059,0.7803921568627451,B.q)
B.bKU=s(["The heart tube starts beating and circulation develops.","Brain, spinal cord, eyes, ears, lungs, gut, and limb buds are rapidly forming.","Facial features and tiny hand/foot plates begin taking shape."],t.s)
B.bbk=s(["The embryo may make tiny spontaneous movements, but they are far too small to feel.","The brain and spinal cord are among the fastest-developing systems right now."],t.s)
B.bMg=s(["Fatigue, nausea, food aversions, smell sensitivity, breast tenderness, and frequent urination are common.","Mood swings can be intense because hormones are rising quickly.","Rest, fluids, bland snacks, and symptom tracking can help you notice patterns."],t.s)
B.c_n=s(["If nausea is rough, aim for \u201csomething gentle\u201d rather than perfect meals.","Protein snacks, ginger, B6 discussions with your clinician, and hydration can be useful.","Keep prenatal vitamin routines as tolerated; ask about alternatives if they worsen nausea."],t.s)
B.bJv=s(["Dating ultrasound or early prenatal intake may happen around this window.","Review medical history, medications, prior pregnancy history, and lab screening plans."],t.s)
B.bI0=s(["Bleeding heavier than spotting, severe cramping, fever, fainting, chest pain, or one-sided pain.","Vomiting with dehydration signs such as very dark urine, dizziness, or inability to keep fluids down."],t.s)
B.aig=new A.ps("Weeks 5\u20138: Heartbeat & foundations","First trimester \xb7 organs forming rapidly","Blueberry / raspberry","0.1\u20130.6 in","<0.1 oz","A curved embryo with early limb buds",B.aBa,B.aA7,B.bKU,B.bbk,B.bMg,B.c_n,B.bJv,B.bI0)
B.axM=new A.k(1,1,0.49411764705882355,0.5803921568627451,B.q)
B.bWO=s(["Baby continues gaining weight and refining lung/brain maturity.","Many babies move head-down during this window, though timing varies.","The immune system receives antibody support through the placenta."],t.s)
B.bR3=s(["Movements may feel slower/stronger because space is tighter, but they should not significantly decrease.","Hiccups, rolls, stretches, and pressure are common sensations."],t.s)
B.bLK=s(["Braxton Hicks, pelvic pressure, back pain, swelling, reflux, and insomnia can be prominent.","Nesting, anxiety, excitement, and impatience can all coexist.","Prepare hospital/birth-center bag, feeding supplies, safe sleep space, and support contacts."],t.s)
B.bP8=s(["Keep meals simple and protein-rich; smaller frequent meals can help reflux.","Fiber and fluids help constipation; iron-rich foods may support late-pregnancy anemia prevention.","Ask about postpartum nutrition if breastfeeding/pumping is planned \u2014 do not assume it if not specified."],t.s)
B.bV5=s(["Review fetal position, GBS testing timing, labor signs, birth plan, pain relief options, and when to call.","Confirm postpartum and newborn visit planning."],t.s)
B.c0F=s(["Reduced movement, bleeding, fluid leakage, regular contractions before 37 weeks, fever, or severe pain.",u.bR],t.s)
B.aih=new A.ps("Weeks 33\u201336: Getting ready","Third trimester \xb7 position, growth & birth prep","Pineapple / romaine lettuce","17\u201318.7 in head-to-heel","4.2\u20135.8 lb","A curled baby with less room to stretch",B.Dv,B.axM,B.bWO,B.bR3,B.bLK,B.bP8,B.bV5,B.c0F)
B.aC4=new A.k(1,0.5450980392156862,0.3607843137254902,1,B.q)
B.azO=new A.k(1,1,0.5607843137254902,0.7411764705882353,B.q)
B.bO2=s(["The embryo is now called a fetus; major organs are present and continue maturing.","Fingers, toes, eyelids, ears, and facial features become more defined.","The placenta is increasingly supporting hormone and nutrient exchange."],t.s)
B.bVV=s(["Baby may stretch, kick, and turn, but most people cannot feel movement yet.","Reflex-like movement begins as nerves and muscles connect."],t.s)
B.c_6=s(["Nausea and fatigue may begin easing near the end of this stage, but not for everyone.","Bloating, constipation, headaches, and breast changes can continue.","Your uterus is growing, though a visible bump may still be subtle."],t.s)
B.bUk=s(["Fiber, fluids, and gentle movement can help constipation.","Iron, calcium, vitamin D, iodine, omega-3s, and protein remain important discussion points.","If appetite returns, rebuild balanced meals gradually."],t.s)
B.bWy=s(["Discuss screening options, lab results, dating, genetic screening, and medication safety.","Ask what symptoms should be reported between visits."],t.s)
B.bFC=s(["Heavy bleeding, severe pain, fever, severe headache, vision changes, fainting, or persistent vomiting.","Any symptom that feels sudden, severe, or frightening."],t.s)
B.aii=new A.ps("Weeks 9\u201312: Looking more baby-like","First trimester \xb7 major structures in place","Strawberry / lime","0.9\u20132.1 in","0.1\u20130.5 oz","A small fetus curled inside the gestational sac",B.aC4,B.azO,B.bO2,B.bVV,B.c_6,B.bUk,B.bWy,B.bFC)
