B.aoa=new A.d8("9-month well-baby visit","Routine well visit",21,"Pediatrician or family doctor","Around 9 months, well visits often focus on growth, feeding progression, sleep, mobility, and communication milestones.","Discuss solids, crawling or early mobility, stranger anxiety, sleep pattern, and communication milestones.","Ask about sleep, solids, mobility, separation anxiety, and communication milestones.",null,B.ak,0)
B.d7J=new A.pR(B.aoa,"Feeding transition follow-up","If solids are hard",14,"Pediatrician or feeding support clinic","Texture progression, gagging, refusal, or intake imbalance may justify extra feeding support in this stage.",!0,"Worth booking if concerns exist",21,"Pediatrician or developmental clinic","Mobility, communication, and social interaction become more noticeable by 9 months and may justify closer review if concerns appear.")
B.anS=new A.d8("4-month well-baby visit and vaccines","Routine well visit",7,"Pediatrician or family doctor","This age range aligns with the 4-month well-baby check, which usually includes growth, development, and scheduled vaccines.","Discuss growth, rolling, head control, laughing, feeding pattern, sleep regression, tummy time, and vaccines due at this visit.","Ask about rolling, head control, sleep changes, crying spikes, feeding amount, and whether any symptom patterns need closer follow-up.",null,B.ak,0)
B.d7K=new A.pR(B.anS,"Feeding and reflux follow-up","If feeds are stressful",7,"Pediatrician and/or lactation consultant","Around 4 months, feeding issues can show up as intake struggle, reflux, bottle refusal, or growth concerns.",!0,"Optional check-in",21,"Pediatrician or developmental clinic","At this age, head control, smiling, rolling, and vocal engagement are common milestone discussion points.")
B.aoe=new A.d8("2-month well-baby visit and vaccines","Routine well visit",7,"Pediatrician or family doctor","At around 2 months, babies typically need a routine well visit with growth, development, and scheduled immunizations based on the CDC childhood timing framework.","Discuss growth, head control, smiling, feeding, sleep, and routine immunizations.","Note feeding volume, sleep pattern, tummy time tolerance, and any congestion, fever, or rash concerns.",null,B.ak,0)
B.d7L=new A.pR(B.aoe,"Feeding support follow-up","If needed",7,"Pediatrician and/or lactation consultant","This stage can still bring latch, bottle-transition, spit-up, or weight-gain questions that justify a feeding follow-up.",!1,"Only if concern appears",21,"Pediatrician","Routine well care usually covers developmental review at this age unless something specific is flagged.")
B.ao3=new A.d8("Age-based pediatric well visit","Routine care",7,"Pediatrician or family doctor","Once birth date is set, Contessa can match the child to the right well-visit window and milestone guidance.","Review growth, feeding, development, sleep, and age-based vaccines or screenings.","Bring feeding, sleep, growth, and milestone questions.",null,B.ak,0)
B.d7M=new A.pR(B.ao3,"Feeding support follow-up","If needed",7,"Pediatrician and/or lactation consultant","Feeding support can matter at any child stage when intake or transfer seems off.",!0,"If milestones feel unclear",21,"Pediatrician or developmental clinic","If milestones feel off, the first step is usually a pediatric developmental review.")
B.anT=new A.d8("24-month well-child visit","Routine well visit",30,"Pediatrician or family doctor","Around 24 months, care often includes language, behavior, growth, sleep, toilet-readiness discussion, and age-based developmental screening.","Discuss speech, pretend play, social interaction, feeding, sleep, behavior, gross motor development, and recommended screenings.","Ask about speech milestones, social interaction, behavior, feeding, toilet readiness, and play skills.",null,B.ak,0)
B.d7N=new A.pR(B.anT,"Toddler feeding or growth support follow-up","If eating or growth concerns are active",21,"Pediatrician or feeding support clinic","By 24 months, ongoing feeding difficulty, poor variety, or growth concerns may justify dedicated feeding follow-up.",!0,"Important if concerns exist",14,u.W,"Speech, social communication, play, behavior, and motor concerns should be reviewed promptly if they stand out by 24 months.")
B.anZ=new A.d8("Toddler well-child visit","Routine well visit",30,"Pediatrician or family doctor","After infancy and early toddlerhood, care continues through well-child visits that monitor growth, development, language, behavior, and vaccines.","Discuss language, motor skills, behavior, sleep, diet, social interaction, and age-based vaccines or screenings.","Ask about language, social interaction, behavior, walking, feeding, and any developmental questions.",null,B.ak,0)
B.d7O=new A.pR(B.anZ,"Feeding support follow-up","If picky eating or intake issues grow",21,"Pediatrician or feeding support clinic","Later toddler stages can bring texture refusal, intake struggles, or persistent mealtime distress.",!0,"Worth booking if concerns exist",21,u.W,"Language, social communication, motor skills, and behavior concerns become important to review through early childhood.")
B.ao5=new A.d8("12-month well-child visit","Routine well visit",30,"Pediatrician or family doctor","Around 12 months, care often includes growth, diet transition, communication milestones, walking progress, and vaccine timing.","Discuss transition from formula or breastmilk balance, sleep, communication, standing or walking, and vaccines due around 12 months.","Ask about speech, walking, transition to cups and solids, sleep, and social engagement.",null,B.ak,0)
B.d7P=new A.pR(B.ao5,"Feeding or texture support follow-up","If eating variety is limited",21,"Pediatrician or feeding support clinic","Feeding support can help if the shift to table foods, cups, or texture progression is difficult.",!0,"Useful if milestones feel delayed",21,"Pediatrician or developmental clinic","Speech, gestures, standing, and early walking concerns often become clearer by this age.")
B.ao6=new A.d8("6-month well-baby visit and vaccines","Routine well visit",14,"Pediatrician or family doctor","Around 6 months, babies typically need a well visit that covers growth, feeding transitions, development, and vaccines.","Review readiness for solids, sleep, motor milestones, rolling, sitting support, and immunizations.","Ask about solid readiness, allergies, sleep pattern, rolling, and next milestone watchpoints.",null,B.ak,0)
B.d7Q=new A.pR(B.ao6,"Feeding transition follow-up","If solids or bottles are difficult",14,"Pediatrician and/or feeding support clinic","As solids approach or begin, feeding questions can shift toward readiness, reflux, stooling, and intake balance.",!0,"Useful if milestone questions are growing",21,"Pediatrician or developmental clinic","This stage often brings questions about sitting, rolling, babbling, and whether development is tracking as expected.")
B.aoh=new A.d8("15-month well-child visit","Routine well visit",30,"Pediatrician or family doctor","Around 15 months, visits often focus on walking progress, language, behavior, sleep, and vaccines due in this period.","Discuss walking, pointing, first words, sleep, tantrums, diet variety, and vaccines or screening due around this stage.","Ask about language, walking, sleep, tantrums, eating variety, and social interaction.",null,B.ak,0)
B.d7R=new A.pR(B.aoh,"Toddler feeding support follow-up","If texture or intake struggles grow",21,"Pediatrician or feeding support clinic","By 15 months, picky eating, bottle weaning, and texture resistance may justify follow-up.",!0,"Worth booking if concerns exist",21,u.W,"Language, pointing, imitation, walking, and social communication become important developmental checkpoints in this stage.")
B.ao2=new A.d8("18-month well-child visit","Routine well visit",30,"Pediatrician or family doctor","Around 18 months, well-child care often includes developmental screening, language review, behavior, growth, and vaccine or screening follow-up depending on the region.","Discuss expressive language, receptive language, walking and climbing, social communication, play skills, sleep, and behavior.","Ask about speech, understanding, social interaction, tantrums, sleep, and whether any screening is recommended now.",null,B.ak,0)
B.d7S=new A.pR(B.ao2,"Toddler feeding support follow-up","If picky eating is limiting growth or family routine",21,"Pediatrician or feeding support clinic","Persistent picky eating, texture refusal, or mealtime distress may need support by 18 months.",!0,"Important if concerns exist",14,u.W,"At 18 months, language, social communication, and behavior concerns often become more visible and can justify formal screening or referral.")
B.aoc=new A.d8("Newborn or 1-month pediatric visit","Routine well visit",7,"Pediatrician or family doctor","Early baby care should include newborn and early weight checks, then a 1-month well visit depending on what has already been completed.","Review weight gain, feeding, jaundice, diaper output, sleep, tummy time, and newborn screening follow-up.","Bring feeding questions, sleep concerns, diaper counts, any jaundice concerns, and fever history.",null,B.ak,0)
B.d7T=new A.pR(B.aoc,"Newborn feeding or weight check","Recommended soon if any concern",4,"Pediatrician and/or lactation consultant","The newborn period is a high-value window for weight checks, feeding transfer review, latch support, and jaundice-linked feeding follow-up.",!1,"Later if needed",21,"Pediatrician","Early development is still mostly tracked within routine newborn care unless a specific concern appears.")
