B.d8Q=new A.pT("Tongue symptoms can relate to irritation, oral thrush, or feeding friction.","Look for white patches that do not wipe away, bleeding, refusal to feed, or worsening discomfort. If the tongue looks coated, sore, or feeding becomes painful or difficult, contact your pediatrician. Keep noting feeding changes and whether the symptom improves or spreads.",null)
